# M-interpolated-strings, panel 121 R4: the form is ONE AST node, desugared in
# the LOWERING and not in the parser — so the formatter re-prints the literal
# as written, and here the IR shows what it became: each text piece a `str`
# constant, each hole that is not already a `str` a `to_str` built-in call, the
# whole chained with `add`. A `str` hole passes through with no call at all,
# which is the ffi seat's condition (no identity call on a `str`).

function main()
    n = 3
    word = "stars"
    s = f"line {n}: {word} and {n + 1}"
    print(s)
